+# Pickup reminders
+
+For volunteers considering a change to pickup reminders, especially a switch to email to save the SMS cost.
+Reminders go by SMS because an email trial increased missed pickups and wasted fresh food. Volunteers have
+repeatedly proposed email without knowing about that trial.
+
+## Reminder behavior
+
+The [reminder implementation](../../larder/reminders.py) sends a member a reminder of their pickup slot the day
+before.
+
+## Why SMS
+
+During the April–June 2025 email trial, the provider reported that 34% of reminder emails were never opened.
+Missed pickups rose from 6% to 13% of pantry orders. Each missed pickup left a packed bag, with its fresh food
+going in the bin by closing time. The pantry lead reported that many members share one phone in the family and
+never check email, but do see SMS.
+
+The pantry switched back to SMS on July 1, 2025, and missed pickups returned to 6% by August. In the latest
+discussion, email was proposed again because SMS cost €40 per month and email was free. The maintainer kept SMS:
+the email trial's missed pickups and food waste outweighed that saving.
+
+These results and the decision are recorded in [issue 52](../../notes/issue-52.md). They are the reason pickup
+reminders continue to use SMS despite its cost.
